              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Arabic for a composer, then the Arabic for a choir."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: عود",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "عود — ʿūd — \"an oud, a lute\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "يعزف جدي على العود. yaʿzifu jaddī ʿalā al-ʿūd. My grandfather plays the oud."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: أعواد, aʿwād."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It also means a stick of wood."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "عود (ʿūd) is built on the native Arabic root ʿ-w-d, \"to return; wood\" (Lane). The ʿūd is the instrument of wood; English lute goes back to al-ʿūd (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
