          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "فرقة (firqa) is built on the native Arabic root f-r-q, \"to separate, to divide\" (Lane). Farq, a difference, which you know, is from the same root: a firqa is a part set apart."
            }
          ]
        },
